      "functional_impact_measured": "Surface immunostaining of non-permeabilized oocytes confirmed cell-surface expression of the HA-tagged construct; transport function of the HA-tagged WT was not separately quantified in the cited paper (used as a trafficking reporter for the Leu275Pro mutant).",
      "confidence": "high",
      "rationale": "L1 explicitly names Pro155 as the insertion point in the second extracellular loop of full-length, membrane-anchored SLC26A1. Python verification confirms residue 155 = P and residue 156 = G, both within ECL2 (138\u2013179), 18 residues from the TM3 C-terminal boundary and 25 residues from the TM4 N-terminal boundary, well clear of the \u22653-residue TM-proximity constraint. Two cysteines (C171, C175) and two potential N-glycosylation sequons (N158, N163) lie downstream of the insertion point, not at it, so the junction itself is free of those constraints. L2 and L3 (same paper, PMC9888379) independently confirm surface display by immunostaining of intact oocytes. Full-length SLC26A1 (WT and Leu275Pro mutant) expressed in Xenopus oocytes; HA epitope inserted by PCR mutagenesis after Pro155 in the second extracellular loop (ECL2, topology residues 138\u2013179). Non-permeabilized PFA-fixed oocytes were immunostained to confirm surface display.",
